# Project conventions

- Stack: Node 22+, pnpm, TypeScript ESM, Express 5, Drizzle/Postgres, Zod, Vitest, Biome.
- Prefer small, focused changes. Match existing naming and folder patterns.
- Do not invent DI frameworks, ORMs, or folder layouts that fight the starter.
- Manual composition only — wire dependencies in `src/app/composition.ts` / module factories.
- Secrets stay out of git; use `.env.example` for new env vars.
- After any user-facing feature, enhancement, or bug fix, update `CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]` (see changelog rule).
- Prefer absolute docs links in README; keep sample `users` module replaceable, not product-specific in docs.

## Commands

- `pnpm dev` / `pnpm worker` / `pnpm jobs:ui` / `pnpm build` / `pnpm test` / `pnpm lint` / `pnpm typecheck`
- DB: `pnpm db:up`, `pnpm db:migrate`
- Docker: `pnpm docker:up` (service names are `api` and `worker`, not `app`)
